From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koels <kyle@tame.gg>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 17:59:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Report per-region blocked time in the benchmark snapshot

Utilisation is wall time inside the tick divided by the interval, not CPU
time, so a region blocked on a lock accrues utilisation exactly as one
doing work does. Summed utilisation rising with thread count therefore
does not establish that more CPU is being burned - which is a conclusion
it is very easy to draw from it, and one this reports cannot support.

missingCPUTimeData is (tick wall time - tick CPU time): the portion of
each tick during which the region thread held no CPU. It is already
computed on every region tick from the ThreadMXBean samples TickTime
carries, so exposing it adds no measurement and no tick-loop cost, and it
separates real parallel work from parallelism overhead.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/gg/tame/silkmc/server/command/RegionStatsSnapshot.java b/src/main/java/gg/tame/silkmc/server/command/RegionStatsSnapshot.java
index e67386f490284245bcddf691ab9a5e3af6bbf2bb..1533ad08077adcbf65975a42ecbd03504a593872 100644
--- a/src/main/java/gg/tame/silkmc/server/command/RegionStatsSnapshot.java
+++ b/src/main/java/gg/tame/silkmc/server/command/RegionStatsSnapshot.java
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@ public final class RegionStatsSnapshot {
     /** One tick window: MSPT figures in milliseconds, plus TPS and the sample count behind them. */
     public record Window(
         int ticks, double tps, double avg, double median, double p95, double p99, double worst,
-        double utilisation
+        double utilisation, double missingCpu
     ) {
         static Window from(final TickData.TickReportData report) {
             if (report == null) {
@@ -73,7 +73,16 @@ public final class RegionStatsSnapshot {
                 ns(mspt.segment5PercentWorst().average()),
                 ns(mspt.segment1PercentWorst().average()),
                 ns(mspt.segmentAll().greatest()),
-                report.utilisation()
+                // Utilisation is WALL time inside the tick divided by the interval - not CPU time. A
+                // region blocked on a lock still accrues utilisation, so a rise in utilisation alone
+                // does not establish that more CPU is being burned.
+                report.utilisation(),
+                // ...which is what this separates out. missingCPUTimeData is (tick wall time - tick CPU
+                // time): time the region thread spent inside its tick while NOT running on a CPU, i.e.
+                // blocked on contention or waiting. It is already computed on every region tick from
+                // the ThreadMXBean samples TickTime carries, so reading it costs nothing extra, and it
+                // is the figure that distinguishes real parallel work from parallelism overhead.
+                ns(report.missingCPUTimeData().segmentAll().average())
             );
         }
 
@@ -97,7 +106,8 @@ public final class RegionStatsSnapshot {
             + " " + prefix + "p95=" + fmt(window.p95())
             + " " + prefix + "p99=" + fmt(window.p99())
             + " " + prefix + "worst=" + fmt(window.worst())
-            + " " + prefix + "util=" + fmt(window.utilisation());
+            + " " + prefix + "util=" + fmt(window.utilisation())
+            + " " + prefix + "blocked=" + fmt(window.missingCpu());
     }
 
     /**
